in a cell; it exists to pull it out.** So it could never have worked for interiors in any coordinate 
space, and the `setParentCell` we told them to call first was being undone by the local apply. 
**Correct primitive was adjacent: `ClientController::sendTransform`** (public, 
`.h:44`/`.cpp:311-340`) â€” branches on `getAttachedTo()` and emits 
`MessageQueueDataTransformWithParent`+`CM_netUpdateTransformWithParent` **carrying the cell id** 
when attached. **Their ORIGINAL sequence was nearly right â€” the only missing piece was telling the 
server;** we sent them chasing a different primitive instead. âš **CONSUMER CONTRACT CHANGE: they 
must now REMOVE `object::setParentCell` around the call** â€” the shim resolves the destination cell 
itself (`findClosestCellObjectFromWorldPosition`â†’`setParentCell`â†’suppressed 
`setTransform_o2p`â†’`objectWarped`â†’`sendTransform`), and an external reparent fights the 
message-variant choice. **STILL UNVERIFIED LIVE â€” ours is offline; if it still reverts, next look 
is `sendTransformUsingParent` (`.h:45`, explicit parent id).** Also on the record: TWO bad calls on 
this row in one day (`getAttachedTo` as mount guard, then `warpClient` as teleport primitive), both 
from reasoning off a name/signature instead of reading what the message does on receipt, both caught 
by consumer live testing. Going forward we state explicitly whether a network-path row was 
live-verified or not.
