The resource model is split differently too: B has global register files plus a separate per-object 
ring, while A’s constant-buffer wrapper exposes generic VS/PS slots and a configurable ring for all 
slot updates. I’m doing one last pass for texture format/mip handling and then I’ll synthesize the 
six requested sections.
