160:	//
161:	// D3DCompile cannot consume D3D9 vertex assembly, so interior/structural/
162:	// sky geometry that ships as `//asm` `.vsh` produced a NULL d3dVS -> the
163:	// draw was skipped (skippedNullVS / [P19SKIP]) -> cell walls/floor/ceiling
164:	// + sky never rendered (handoff facet 5). The PIXEL path already has a
165:	// fallback (Phase 17: selectFallbackPSForVS -> buildHlslForVSOutputs); the
166:	// VERTEX path had none. This generic HLSL VS restores the symmetry: it
167:	// applies the standard object->clip WVP (objectWorldCameraProjectionMatrix
168:	// @ b0 c0 -- the exact transform3d() the //hlsl VS use, row-vector mul +
169:	// PACK_MATRIX_ROW_MAJOR to match the transposed upload) and forwards
170:	// TEXCOORD0, emitting a CONST WHITE COLOR0 so the reflection-driven
171:	// fallback PS samples t0/s0 * white = the diffuse texture. Design:
172:	// .planning/research/CONSULT-19-vs-fallback-interior-asm-SYNTHESIS.md
173:	// (CODEX + Cursor converged, code-grounded).
174:	//
175:	// Input is MINIMAL (POSITION0 + TEXCOORD0 only): missing semantics are
176:	// backed by phantom-zero elements at slot 15 (augmentWithPhantomElements).
