row(s) at register %d runs past the end of the %d-row register file.", numberOfConstants, index, 
cms_pixelRows));
331:
332:	if (!numberOfConstants)
333:		return;
334:
335:	int const bytes = numberOfConstants * cms_bytesPerRow;
336:	float * const destination = ms_pixelShadow + (index * 4);
377: * On the ring path this appends at the cursor with WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE, which does
378: * not rename the buffer, and binds a sub-range by offset. That is the whole point:
379: * a draw costs sixteen bytes of bookkeeping rather than a buffer rename.
380: *
381: * On the fallback path it renames one of a handful of small buffers with DISCARD
382: * and binds it whole.
