branch.

**1. Device / Context Model**
Repo A: `Direct3d11_Device` owns device, swap chain, immediate context, back-buffer RTV, depth 
texture/DSV as file-scope `ComPtr`s; it creates a hardware FL11.0 device via `D3D11CreateDevice` and 
stores the immediate context returned by that call ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-cli
ent-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:449), [Direct3d11_Dev
ice.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d1
1_Device.cpp:456)). Swap chain creation is in the same file via `CreateSwapChainForHwnd`, flip 
discard, BGRA8, two buffers ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/clien
t/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:581), [Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/C
ode/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:595)). 
Back-buffer RTV and D24S8 DSV are created together ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-cli
ent-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:356), [Direct3d11_Dev
ice.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d1
1_Device.cpp:364), [Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/applicat
ion/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:380)). Resize clears state, releases RTV/DSV, calls 
`ResizeBuffers`, recreates views ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/
client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:1292)). Present treats removed/reset 
as fatal, no recovery ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/appl
ication/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:1214)). No deferred-context creation found; only 
immediate context ownership is evidenced ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src
/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:74)).

Repo B: splits device and swap chain. `Direct3d11_Device` owns `ID3D11Device1` and 
`ID3D11DeviceContext1`, querying both from the base objects returned by `D3D11CreateDevice` (B 
`Direct3d11_Device.cpp:226-248`). `Direct3d11_SwapChain` owns swap chain/back-buffer/depth views, 
creates flip-discard with optional tearing fallback (B `Direct3d11_SwapChain.cpp:145-160`), creates 
back-buffer RTV and tries D24S8 then D32S8 depth-stencil formats (B 
`Direct3d11_SwapChain.cpp:179-235`). Resize fires engine device-lost callbacks, releases back-buffer 
views, resizes, recreates views, and resizes scene target (B `Direct3d11_SwapChain.cpp:655-670`). 
Present supports tearing and occlusion; removed/reset is checked via 
`Direct3d11_Device::checkForDeviceRemoved` (B `Direct3d11_SwapChain.cpp:608-628`). No 
deferred-context creation found; context is immediate `ID3D11DeviceContext1` (B 
`Direct3d11_Device.cpp:29`, `:247`).

Divergences: A is monolithic in `Device` and fatal on most swap-chain failures; B separates 
`Device`/`SwapChain`, uses D3D11.1 interfaces pervasively, supports tearing/occlusion paths, and 
explicitly fires device-lost/restored registries on resize.

**2. State Management**
Repo A: state object caches live inside `Direct3d11_StateCache` as `unordered_map<uint64_t, 
ComPtr<...>>` for raster/blend/depth/sampler ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-clien
t-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:105)). State 
creation is internal 
`CreateRasterizerState/CreateBlendState/CreateDepthStencilState/CreateSamplerState` ([Direct3d11_Stat
eCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct
3d11_StateCache.cpp:901)). It tracks bound SRVs/samplers and flushes arrays before draw ([Direct3d11_
StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Di
rect3d11_StateCache.cpp:135), [Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/
client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:1449)). Static shader passes push 
alpha/depth/sampler/SRV state into StateCache rather than binding directly ([Direct3d11_StaticShaderD
ata.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d1
1_StaticShaderData.cpp:1664), [Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/e
ngine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:1731), [Direct3d11_Stat
icShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/
Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:1838)).

Repo B: state object creation is factored into `Direct3d11_StateObjectCache`, keyed by full D3D11 
descriptor bytes using `std::map<D3D11_*_DESC,..., ByteLess>` for blend/depth/sampler, while 
rasterizer states are pre-indexed by fill/cull/scissor (B `Direct3d11_StateObjectCache.cpp:36-48`). 
It has max-cache fatal guards and creates states on cache miss (B 
`Direct3d11_StateObjectCache.cpp:156-220`). Binding redundancy is handled by 
`Direct3d11_StateCache`, which shadows current pointers and skips identical bind calls (B 
`Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:186-261`). B also has an explicit “no invalidate” design: all shadowed 
state must be set through the cache (B `Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:168-183`).

Divergences: A’s state-object cache is embedded and uses compact integer keys; B’s is a separate 
descriptor-keyed subsystem with stricter descriptor identity and cache-size assertions. B’s 
separation is structurally cleaner on evidence; A has more accumulated pass-specific state 
compatibility in the same cache.

**3. Shader System**
Repo A: compiles HLSL through `D3DCompile` with D3DCompile-era rewriting and `.cso` cache support. 
Cache is persistent, source-hash keyed, macro-aware ([Direct3d11_ShaderCache.h](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg
-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_ShaderCache.h:6)). A has an 
assembly VS fallback that generates generic HLSL for `//asm` vertex programs, using WVP and 
TEXCOORD0, with documented limitations ([Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-clien
t-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp:161), [Direct
3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/s
rc/win32/Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp:181)). It also dynamically generates pixel shaders that 
mirror the active VS output signature register-for-register, compiling/cacheing by VS bytecode hash (
[Direct3d11_PixelShaderProgramData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application
/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_PixelShaderProgramData.cpp:1486)). Static shader data bridges 
engine `StaticShader`/`ShaderImplementation` passes into D3D11 state and shader data ([Direct3d11_Sta
ticShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32
/Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:386)).

Repo B: splits shader source transformation, compile, cache, reflection, and signatures into 
separate files. Compiler flags are `D3DCOMPILE_ENABLE_BACKWARDS_COMPATIBILITY | 
D3DCOMPILE_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL3`, explicitly no `PACK_MATRIX_ROW_MAJOR` (B 
`Direct3d11_ShaderCompiler.cpp:35-37`). `ShaderSource` documents nine source transforms, including 
fixed-function alpha/fog epilogue and D3DCompile incompatibility repairs (B 
`Direct3d11_ShaderSource.h:6-24`). It explicitly does not translate assembly; `//asm` or `ps.1.x` is 
refused because D3DCompile has no assembler (B `Direct3d11_ShaderSource.h:104-106`). Pixel/vertex 
program objects compile source through `Direct3d11_ShaderCompiler`, reflect bytecode, then create 
shader objects (B `Direct3d11_PixelShaderProgramData.cpp:88-122`, B 
`Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp:170-206`). B’s shader cache is content-keyed on exact prepared 
D3DCompile input and validates include hashes via a manifest (B `Direct3d11_ShaderCache.h:18-38`, B 
`Direct3d11_ShaderCache.cpp:62-209`).

Divergences: A includes runtime fallback/generation for assembly VS and per-VS fallback PS. B 
refuses shader assembly and appears to depend on converted asset HLSL being present. B’s shader 
pipeline is more modular and documented; A has more runtime compatibility fallback for mixed/legacy 
shader assets.

**4. Constant Buffers**
Repo A: generic `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer` exposes VS/PS slots. It has a config-gated D3D11.1 
`NO_OVERWRITE` ring for all slot updates: append fixed 1280-byte entries and bind subranges with 
`*SetConstantBuffers1`; fallback is per-slot dynamic buffers with `Map(WRITE_DISCARD)` ([Direct3d11_C
onstantBuffer.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32
/Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp:108), [Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/
src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp:184), [Direct3d11_Co
nstantBuffer.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/
Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp:425)). VS slot 0 is a CPU shadow, with engine register writes copied 
by `registerIndex * 16`; it flushes once per draw ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-
client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:337), [Direct3
d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win3
2/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:521), [Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/eng
ine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:1281)). A transposes WVP/world 
before storing to match its row-vector shader convention ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Co
de/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:387)).

Repo B: `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers` models shader constants as CPU-shadowed D3D9-style register 
files: `b0` globals rows 0..95, `b1` pixel epilogue, `b3` per-object matrices in a ring (B 
`Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers.h:6-28`). Setters keep D3D9 signature: register index plus row count; 
dirty rows are tracked with memcmp/coalescing (B `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers.cpp:298-321`). 
Per-object matrices use a D3D11.1 `WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE` ring, fallback rotating `WRITE_DISCARD` 
buffers (B `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers.cpp:377-444`). Globals flush whole shadows with 
`WRITE_DISCARD`, explicitly avoiding partial DISCARD undefined-tail bugs (B 
`Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers.cpp:574-634`). B explicitly does no matrix transposes and documents why: 
it ports only the VSPS path and relies on column-major packing/backwards compatibility preserving 
register offsets (B `Direct3d11_Transforms.h:24-36`).

Divergences: A transposes matrices and has a generic all-slot cbuffer ring; B keeps untransposed 
VSPS bytes, separates globals/epilogue/per-object, and rings only the hot per-object slice. B’s 
model is more explicitly tied to the engine register ABI; A’s model is more generalized and has 
broader ring coverage.

**5. Vertex / Index Buffers**
Repo A: static VBs are `D3D11_USAGE_DEFAULT`; lock returns CPU staging, unlock `UpdateSubresource`, 
