 [Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d1
1/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:86)). Resource usage maps render-target/dynamic/static to 
D3D11 usage/bind flags; static uses `UpdateSubresource` via lock/unlock because engine fills after 
creation ([Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/
Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:282)). Dynamic 2D textures map directly; others use 
staging ([Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/D
irect3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:609)). Render-target RTVs are cached per texture to 
avoid recreate churn ([Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/
application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:1039)). SRV binding maps engine D3D9 
stage to reflected PS texture slot, with samplers kept at stage index ([Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.c
pp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Sta
ticShaderData.cpp:1813)).

Repo B: texture code documents three formats: native, storage, DXGI; TF_L_8 is stored expanded 
because DXGI lacks L8 sampling as `(L,L,L,1)` (B `Direct3d11_TextureData.h:31-47`). Uploads always 
use per-lock scratch buffer to honor engine pitch and cube/mip lock semantics (B 
`Direct3d11_TextureData.h:16-28`). It tracks initialized subresources to avoid readback stalls on 
first mip upload (B `Direct3d11_TextureData.h:50-57`, B `Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:307-309`, 
`:838-853`). Creates 2D/3D/cube resources, render targets also shader resources (B 
`Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:418-470`). Unlock handles block-compressed whole-level writes with null 
