I read the locked evidence first and traced Repo A working tree plus Repo B at `origin/x64-dx11-vanilla`. Repo B citations refer to `D:\Code\Galaxies-Reborn\client-tools` on that branch.

**1. Device / Context Model**
Repo A: `Direct3d11_Device` owns device, swap chain, immediate context, back-buffer RTV, depth texture/DSV as file-scope `ComPtr`s; it creates a hardware FL11.0 device via `D3D11CreateDevice` and stores the immediate context returned by that call ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:449), [Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:456)). Swap chain creation is in the same file via `CreateSwapChainForHwnd`, flip discard, BGRA8, two buffers ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:581), [Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:595)). Back-buffer RTV and D24S8 DSV are created together ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:356), [Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:364), [Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:380)). Resize clears state, releases RTV/DSV, calls `ResizeBuffers`, recreates views ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:1292)). Present treats removed/reset as fatal, no recovery ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:1214)). No deferred-context creation found; only immediate context ownership is evidenced ([Direct3d11_Device.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_Device.cpp:74)).

Repo B: splits device and swap chain. `Direct3d11_Device` owns `ID3D11Device1` and `ID3D11DeviceContext1`, querying both from the base objects returned by `D3D11CreateDevice` (B `Direct3d11_Device.cpp:226-248`). `Direct3d11_SwapChain` owns swap chain/back-buffer/depth views, creates flip-discard with optional tearing fallback (B `Direct3d11_SwapChain.cpp:145-160`), creates back-buffer RTV and tries D24S8 then D32S8 depth-stencil formats (B `Direct3d11_SwapChain.cpp:179-235`). Resize fires engine device-lost callbacks, releases back-buffer views, resizes, recreates views, and resizes scene target (B `Direct3d11_SwapChain.cpp:655-670`). Present supports tearing and occlusion; removed/reset is checked via `Direct3d11_Device::checkForDeviceRemoved` (B `Direct3d11_SwapChain.cpp:608-628`). No deferred-context creation found; context is immediate `ID3D11DeviceContext1` (B `Direct3d11_Device.cpp:29`, `:247`).

Divergences: A is monolithic in `Device` and fatal on most swap-chain failures; B separates `Device`/`SwapChain`, uses D3D11.1 interfaces pervasively, supports tearing/occlusion paths, and explicitly fires device-lost/restored registries on resize.

**2. State Management**
Repo A: state object caches live inside `Direct3d11_StateCache` as `unordered_map<uint64_t, ComPtr<...>>` for raster/blend/depth/sampler ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:105)). State creation is internal `CreateRasterizerState/CreateBlendState/CreateDepthStencilState/CreateSamplerState` ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:901)). It tracks bound SRVs/samplers and flushes arrays before draw ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:135), [Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:1449)). Static shader passes push alpha/depth/sampler/SRV state into StateCache rather than binding directly ([Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:1664), [Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:1731), [Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:1838)).

Repo B: state object creation is factored into `Direct3d11_StateObjectCache`, keyed by full D3D11 descriptor bytes using `std::map<D3D11_*_DESC,..., ByteLess>` for blend/depth/sampler, while rasterizer states are pre-indexed by fill/cull/scissor (B `Direct3d11_StateObjectCache.cpp:36-48`). It has max-cache fatal guards and creates states on cache miss (B `Direct3d11_StateObjectCache.cpp:156-220`). Binding redundancy is handled by `Direct3d11_StateCache`, which shadows current pointers and skips identical bind calls (B `Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:186-261`). B also has an explicit “no invalidate” design: all shadowed state must be set through the cache (B `Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:168-183`).

Divergences: A’s state-object cache is embedded and uses compact integer keys; B’s is a separate descriptor-keyed subsystem with stricter descriptor identity and cache-size assertions. B’s separation is structurally cleaner on evidence; A has more accumulated pass-specific state compatibility in the same cache.

**3. Shader System**
Repo A: compiles HLSL through `D3DCompile` with D3DCompile-era rewriting and `.cso` cache support. Cache is persistent, source-hash keyed, macro-aware ([Direct3d11_ShaderCache.h](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_ShaderCache.h:6)). A has an assembly VS fallback that generates generic HLSL for `//asm` vertex programs, using WVP and TEXCOORD0, with documented limitations ([Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp:161), [Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp:181)). It also dynamically generates pixel shaders that mirror the active VS output signature register-for-register, compiling/cacheing by VS bytecode hash ([Direct3d11_PixelShaderProgramData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_PixelShaderProgramData.cpp:1486)). Static shader data bridges engine `StaticShader`/`ShaderImplementation` passes into D3D11 state and shader data ([Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:386)).

Repo B: splits shader source transformation, compile, cache, reflection, and signatures into separate files. Compiler flags are `D3DCOMPILE_ENABLE_BACKWARDS_COMPATIBILITY | D3DCOMPILE_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL3`, explicitly no `PACK_MATRIX_ROW_MAJOR` (B `Direct3d11_ShaderCompiler.cpp:35-37`). `ShaderSource` documents nine source transforms, including fixed-function alpha/fog epilogue and D3DCompile incompatibility repairs (B `Direct3d11_ShaderSource.h:6-24`). It explicitly does not translate assembly; `//asm` or `ps.1.x` is refused because D3DCompile has no assembler (B `Direct3d11_ShaderSource.h:104-106`). Pixel/vertex program objects compile source through `Direct3d11_ShaderCompiler`, reflect bytecode, then create shader objects (B `Direct3d11_PixelShaderProgramData.cpp:88-122`, B `Direct3d11_VertexShaderData.cpp:170-206`). B’s shader cache is content-keyed on exact prepared D3DCompile input and validates include hashes via a manifest (B `Direct3d11_ShaderCache.h:18-38`, B `Direct3d11_ShaderCache.cpp:62-209`).

Divergences: A includes runtime fallback/generation for assembly VS and per-VS fallback PS. B refuses shader assembly and appears to depend on converted asset HLSL being present. B’s shader pipeline is more modular and documented; A has more runtime compatibility fallback for mixed/legacy shader assets.

**4. Constant Buffers**
Repo A: generic `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer` exposes VS/PS slots. It has a config-gated D3D11.1 `NO_OVERWRITE` ring for all slot updates: append fixed 1280-byte entries and bind subranges with `*SetConstantBuffers1`; fallback is per-slot dynamic buffers with `Map(WRITE_DISCARD)` ([Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp:108), [Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp:184), [Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_ConstantBuffer.cpp:425)). VS slot 0 is a CPU shadow, with engine register writes copied by `registerIndex * 16`; it flushes once per draw ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:337), [Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:521), [Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:1281)). A transposes WVP/world before storing to match its row-vector shader convention ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:387)).

Repo B: `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers` models shader constants as CPU-shadowed D3D9-style register files: `b0` globals rows 0..95, `b1` pixel epilogue, `b3` per-object matrices in a ring (B `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers.h:6-28`). Setters keep D3D9 signature: register index plus row count; dirty rows are tracked with memcmp/coalescing (B `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers.cpp:298-321`). Per-object matrices use a D3D11.1 `WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE` ring, fallback rotating `WRITE_DISCARD` buffers (B `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers.cpp:377-444`). Globals flush whole shadows with `WRITE_DISCARD`, explicitly avoiding partial DISCARD undefined-tail bugs (B `Direct3d11_ConstantBuffers.cpp:574-634`). B explicitly does no matrix transposes and documents why: it ports only the VSPS path and relies on column-major packing/backwards compatibility preserving register offsets (B `Direct3d11_Transforms.h:24-36`).

Divergences: A transposes matrices and has a generic all-slot cbuffer ring; B keeps untransposed VSPS bytes, separates globals/epilogue/per-object, and rings only the hot per-object slice. B’s model is more explicitly tied to the engine register ABI; A’s model is more generalized and has broader ring coverage.

**5. Vertex / Index Buffers**
Repo A: static VBs are `D3D11_USAGE_DEFAULT`; lock returns CPU staging, unlock `UpdateSubresource`, then persists CPU shadow for later read-only locks ([Direct3d11_StaticVertexBufferData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StaticVertexBufferData.cpp:8), [Direct3d11_StaticVertexBufferData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StaticVertexBufferData.cpp:167)). Dynamic VBs/IBs are shared rings using `WRITE_DISCARD` on wrap/new frame and `WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE` otherwise ([Direct3d11_DynamicVertexBufferData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_DynamicVertexBufferData.cpp:259), [Direct3d11_DynamicIndexBufferData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_DynamicIndexBufferData.cpp:118)). Input layouts are cached in `Direct3d11_VertexDeclarationMap` by VB format plus VS variant bytecode hash; multi-stream path has its own cache ([Direct3d11_VertexDeclarationMap.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_VertexDeclarationMap.cpp:190), [Direct3d11_VertexDeclarationMap.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_VertexDeclarationMap.cpp:320)). It binds a phantom zero VB at slot 15 for missing VS inputs ([Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StateCache.cpp:1335)).

Repo B: static VBs likewise use `USAGE_DEFAULT + UpdateSubresource`, with CPU shadow matching D3DPOOL_MANAGED semantics (B `Direct3d11_StaticVertexBufferData.h:18-25`, B `Direct3d11_StaticVertexBufferData.cpp:84-90`, `:166-170`). Dynamic VBs use a process ring plus system-memory mirror; lock returns scratch, unlock copies to GPU with `WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE`; discard happens at lock time when DX9 would discard (B `Direct3d11_DynamicVertexBufferData.cpp:24-31`, `:168-217`, `:229-245`). Draw binding and input layout resolution are split into `Direct3d11_Draw`; input layouts come from `Direct3d11_InputLayoutCache` using stream formats, VS bytecode/signature hash, and texture-coordinate mapping (B `Direct3d11_Draw.cpp:435-445`). B also supports multi-stream binding explicitly (B `Direct3d11_Draw.cpp:217-288`).

Divergences: Both converge on static CPU shadows and dynamic rings. A’s draw/input-layout logic is inside `StateCache` and includes phantom-slot fallback; B splits drawing into `Direct3d11_Draw` and has a more explicit system-memory mirror/ring discipline.

**6. Textures**
Repo A: texture format mapping is an inline `translationTable`, with unsupported formats as `DXGI_FORMAT_UNKNOWN` and block-compression padding logic ([Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:52), [Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:86)). Resource usage maps render-target/dynamic/static to D3D11 usage/bind flags; static uses `UpdateSubresource` via lock/unlock because engine fills after creation ([Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:282)). Dynamic 2D textures map directly; others use staging ([Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:609)). Render-target RTVs are cached per texture to avoid recreate churn ([Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:1039)). SRV binding maps engine D3D9 stage to reflected PS texture slot, with samplers kept at stage index ([Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp](/abs/path/D:/Code/swg-client-v2/src/engine/client/application/Direct3d11/src/win32/Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:1813)).

Repo B: texture code documents three formats: native, storage, DXGI; TF_L_8 is stored expanded because DXGI lacks L8 sampling as `(L,L,L,1)` (B `Direct3d11_TextureData.h:31-47`). Uploads always use per-lock scratch buffer to honor engine pitch and cube/mip lock semantics (B `Direct3d11_TextureData.h:16-28`). It tracks initialized subresources to avoid readback stalls on first mip upload (B `Direct3d11_TextureData.h:50-57`, B `Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:307-309`, `:838-853`). Creates 2D/3D/cube resources, render targets also shader resources (B `Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:418-470`). Unlock handles block-compressed whole-level writes with null box, partial compressed alignment checks, conversion through `Direct3d11_TextureConverter`, then `UpdateSubresource` (B `Direct3d11_TextureData.cpp:891-982`). Static shader binding maps sampler stage to reflected texture slot and validates SRV dimension mismatch (B `Direct3d11_StaticShaderData.cpp:644-692`).

Divergences: A has direct mapping/conversion in `TextureData` plus cached RTVs; B has a more formal native/storage/DXGI format model, initialized-subresource tracking, explicit converter subsystem, volume/cube documentation, and SRV dimension validation. B is more complete on texture evidence.

| subsystem | A approach | B approach | divergent? | more complete on evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Device/context | Monolithic `Device` owns device/swap/context/RTV/DSV; fatal removed/reset; resize in same file | Split `Device` + `SwapChain`; D3D11.1 context; tearing/occlusion; fires lost/restored on resize | Yes | B |
| State management | Embedded `StateCache` caches by compact integer keys; broad pass compatibility in cache | Separate descriptor-keyed `StateObjectCache` plus pointer-shadow bind cache | Yes | B structurally; A has more compatibility patches |
| Shader system | D3DCompile + source rewrite + persistent `.cso`; runtime assembly VS fallback and generated fallback PS | Modular source/compiler/reflection/signature/cache; refuses assembly; depends on converted HLSL | Yes | A for runtime legacy fallback; B for modularity |
| Constant buffers | Generic VS/PS slot wrapper; all-slot D3D11.1 `NO_OVERWRITE` ring; transposes matrices | D3D9 register-file shadows; separate globals/epilogue/per-object ring; no transposes | Yes | B for ABI clarity; A for broader ring coverage |
| VB/IB/input layout | Static shadows + UpdateSubresource; dynamic rings; input layouts in `VertexDeclarationMap`; phantom zero slot | Static shadows + UpdateSubresource; dynamic ring with scratch mirror; draw/input layouts split into `Draw`/`InputLayoutCache` | Yes, mostly organization/details | Insufficient evidence; both comparable |
| Textures | Inline format table; dynamic map/staging; cached RTVs; reflected stage→SRV remap | Native/storage/DXGI model; converter subsystem; initialized-subresource tracking; cube/volume handling; dimension validation | Yes | B |
